    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="7.3">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IIIAs">III As</ref> 7.3</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="7.3" corresp="#wit-q">Et si dominus uel prepositus uel aliquis homo hoc infringat uel abhinc exeat, sit dignus eorum que apud Greateleiam dicta sunt, nisi regi placeat (magis) alia iusticia.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" n="7.3" corresp="#wit-q">Et si [dominus vel] præpositus vel aliquis homo hoc infringat vel abhinc exeat, sit dignus eorum quæ apud Greateleiam dicta sunt, nisi regi [magis] placeat alia iustitia.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-q">And if a lord or a reeve or any man breaks this decree or departs from it, he shall suffer the penalties declared at Grately, unless the king prefers to inflict a different penalty.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="170"><ref target="clause:IIAs_25-2">II As 25.2</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">Vgl. II As[?] 25, 2</note>
        <note type="comparisonIncomplete">Some of Liebermann’s notes here are cut off in the gutter of the scan used, and are still to be completed.</note>
        <note type="editorial">Latin only; no German translation in Liebermann. ‘dominus uel’ is missing from K and written above the line in Co. Liebermann compares II As 25.</note>
      </div>
    </body>
